{#
  The mail-merge « Variable » control, slotted into
  partials/rich_text_form_field.html.twig's extra toolbar row.

  One entry per column of the imported file, with the first row's value
  as a sample hint — « Prénom » next to « Kaa » tells a chief which
  column is which far better than its header alone. Inserting from here
  rather than typing is the whole point: a mistyped column name is a
  variable that never substitutes, and the recipient reads the braces.

  Hidden until an audience is attached (there is nothing to offer
  otherwise) and while the email is no longer a draft.
#}
{% if audience and editable %}
    <div class="dropdown mb-2" id="mm-variable-dropdown">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary dropdown-toggle" data-bs-toggle="dropdown"
                title="Insérer une variable du fichier de publipostage">
            <i class="bi bi-braces" aria-hidden="true"></i> Variable
        </button>
        <ul class="dropdown-menu" id="mm-variable-menu" style="max-height: 20rem; overflow-y: auto;">
            {% for column in audience.columns %}
                <li>
                    <button type="button" class="dropdown-item d-flex justify-content-between gap-3 mm-variable-item"
                            data-column="{{ column }}">
                        <span>{{ column }}</span>
                        <span class="text-body-secondary small text-truncate" style="max-width: 10rem;">
                            « {{ audience_sample[column]|default('—') ?: '—' }} »
                        </span>
                    </button>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </div>
{% endif %}
